    !---------------------------------------------
    ! hipblasDotEx
    !---------------------------------------------
    !>     \brief  BLAS EX API
    !>
    !>     \details
    !>     The dotEx functions perform the dot product of vectors ``x`` and ``y``:
    !>
    !>         result = x * y;
    !>
    !>     The dotcEx functions perform the dot product of the conjugate of complex vector ``x`` and
    !>     complex vector ``y``:
    !>
    !>         result = conjugate (x) * y;
    !>
    !>     The supported types are determined by the backend. See the rocBLAS or cuBLAS
    !>     documentation.
    !>
    !>     @param[in] handle - [hipblasHandle_t]
    !>               handle to the hipBLAS library context queue.
    !>     @param[in] n - [int]
    !>               the number of elements in x and y.
    !>     @param[in] x - device pointer storing vector x.
    !>     @param[in] xType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>               specifies the datatype of vector x.
    !>     @param[in] incx - [int]
    !>               specifies the increment for the elements of y.
    !>     @param[in] y - device pointer storing vector y.
    !>     @param[in] yType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>               specifies the datatype of vector y.
    !>     @param[in] incy - [int]
    !>               specifies the increment for the elements of y.
    !>     @param[inout] myResult
    !>               device pointer or host pointer to store the dot product.
    !>               Return value is 0.0 if n <= 0.
    !>     @param[in] resultType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>               specifies the datatype of the result.
    !>     @param[in] executionType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>               specifies the datatype of computation.
