    !---------------------------------------------
    ! hipblasRotEx
    !---------------------------------------------
    !>  \brief  BLAS EX API
    !>
    !>     \details
    !>     The rotEx functions applies the Givens rotation matrix defined by ``c=cos(alpha)`` and
    !>     ``s=sin(alpha)`` to vectors ``x`` and ``y``.
    !>     Scalars ``c`` and ``s`` can be stored in either the host or device memory. The location
    !>     is specified by calling ``hipblasSetPointerMode``.
    !>
    !>     If ``cs_type`` is real:
    !>
    !>         x := c * x + s * y
    !>         y := c * y - s * x
    !>
    !>     If ``cs_type`` is complex, the imaginary part of ``c`` is ignored:
    !>
    !>         x := real(c) * x + s * y
    !>         y := real(c) * y - conj(s) * x
    !>
    !>     The supported types are determined by the backend. See the rocBLAS or cuBLAS
    !>     documentation.
    !>
    !>     @param[in] handle - [hipblasHandle_t]
    !>             handle to the hipBLAS library context queue.
    !>     @param[in] n - [int]
    !>             number of elements in the x and y vectors.
    !>     @param[inout] x - device pointer storing vector x.
    !>     @param[in] xType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>             specifies the datatype of vector x.
    !>     @param[in] incx - [int]
    !>             specifies the increment between elements of x.
    !>     @param[inout] y - device pointer storing vector y.
    !>     @param[in] yType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>             specifies the datatype of vector y.
    !>     @param[in] incy - [int]
    !>             specifies the increment between elements of y.
    !>     @param[in] c - device pointer or host pointer storing scalar cosine component of the
    !>     rotation matrix.
    !>     @param[in] s - device pointer or host pointer storing scalar sine component of the
    !>     rotation matrix.
    !>     @param[in] csType
    !>     [hipDataType]
    !>             specifies the datatype of c and s.
    !>     @param[in] executionType
    !>     [hipDataType]
